From cec2036081893ca20ba7906dbb59e168da21bc57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: exynos9820: add CMU_PERIC1, CMU_AUD,
 pll_0831x_k3, CLKOUT

Clocks the Galaxy S10 family needs on top of the Exynos 9820 clock
driver:

 - CMU_PERIC1: muxes, dividers and gates of UART_BT, USI07/08/10/16/17
   with their USI_I2C blocks and the camera I2C_CAM0..3 blocks.
 - CMU_AUD: audio PLL, ABOX core, UAIF/DSIF bit clocks and their
   gates, for the ABOX audio DSP.
 - pll_0831x_k3: on Exynos 9820 PMS, ENABLE and STABLE of the 0831x
   PLL live in PLL_CON0 and K in PLL_CON3 (three registers further
   instead of two), so PLL_AUD0 needs a PLL type that only moves the K
   register.
 - exynos-clkout: the Exynos 9820 PMU clock outputs, CLKOUT0, and
   CLKOUT1 as a gate whose parent is the PMU node's "tcxo" clock (it
   feeds the NFC controller).

The binding IDs are part of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos-clkout.c |  83 +++-
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c    | 605 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c           |  17 +-
